sequenceDiagram
    participant P as touch event
    participant STATS as KeyTouchStats (bounded online stats)
    participant GEOM as HitGeometry (ellipse model)
    participant KEY as key resolution (views.rs key_at)
    participant OPT as optimizer (low-priority pass)
    participant UI as UI preview

    P->>STATS: constant/bounded-time update (Welford)
    P->>KEY: resolve intended key (current HitGeometry)
    KEY-->>P: key action (normal handling)

    Note over OPT: after sufficient samples / scheduled pass
    OPT->>OPT: candidate layouts minimize expected input cost
    OPT->>OPT: enforce constraints (displacement, overlap, boundary)
    OPT-->>GEOM: effective geometry update (hysteresis-bounded)
    OPT-->>UI: explainability diagnostics (sample count, bias, constraint)

    Note over GEOM: freeze -> no pass mutates geometry until unfrozen
